---@field metadata? kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApimachineryPkgApisMetaV1ObjectMeta metadata is the standard object metadata. metadata.name must be the Kubernetes node name.
---@field spec? kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1CSINodeSpec spec is the specification of CSINode
---@field status? kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1CSINodeStatus status contains health and status information for the node's storage.

---CSINodeDriver holds information about the specification of one CSI driver installed on a node
---@class kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1CSINodeDriver
---@field allocatable? kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1VolumeNodeResources allocatable represents the volume resources of a node that are available for scheduling. This field is beta.
---@field name string name represents the name of the CSI driver that this object refers to. This MUST be the same name returned by the CSI GetPluginName() call for that driver.
---@field nodeID string nodeID of the node from the driver point of view. This field enables Kubernetes to communicate with storage systems that do not share the same nomenclature for nodes. For example, Kubernetes may refer to a given node as "node1", but the storage system may refer to the same node as "nodeA". When Kubernetes issues a command to the storage system to attach a volume to a specific node, it can use this field to refer to the node name using the ID that the storage system will understand, e.g. "nodeA" instead of "node1". This field is required.
---@field topologyKeys? kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1CSINodeDriverTopologyKeysList topologyKeys is the list of keys supported by the driver. When a driver is initialized on a cluster, it provides a set of topology keys that it understands (e.g. "company.com/zone", "company.com/region"). When a driver is initialized on a node, it provides the same topology keys along with values. Kubelet will expose these topology keys as labels on its own node object. When Kubernetes does topology aware provisioning, it can use this list to determine which labels it should retrieve from the node object and pass back to the driver. It is possible for different nodes to use different topology keys. This can be empty if driver does not support topology.

---topologyKeys is the list of keys supported by the driver. When a driver is initialized on a cluster, it provides a set of topology keys that it understands (e.g. "company.com/zone", "company.com/region"). When a driver is initialized on a node, it provides the same topology keys along with values. Kubelet will expose these topology keys as labels on its own node object. When Kubernetes does topology aware provisioning, it can use this list to determine which labels it should retrieve from the node object and pass back to the driver. It is possible for different nodes to use different topology keys. This can be empty if driver does not support topology.
---@alias kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1CSINodeDriverTopologyKeysList string[]

