---StorageHealth contains storage backend health reported by a CSI driver on a node.
---@class kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1StorageHealth
---@field healthConditions? kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1StorageHealthHealthConditionsList healthConditions are the storage backend conditions reported by the CSI driver. At most 16 conditions may be reported. An empty list means the CSI driver either does not support storage health or has not reported it yet. If the driver supports storage health and its storage backend is healthy, the kubelet reports a StorageHealthy condition.
---@field name string name is the CSI driver name, matching CSINodeDriver.name.

---StorageHealthCondition represents a health condition reported by a CSI driver for its storage backend on a node.
---@class kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1StorageHealthCondition
---@field accessMode? string accessMode is the access mode affected. Nil means all access modes are affected.
---@field lastTransitionTime? string lastTransitionTime is when this condition first appeared at its current state. lastTransitionTime remains unchanged when only the message changes.
---@field message? string message is a human-readable description. Maximum permitted length of a message is 1024 bytes.
---@field reason string reason is a brief CamelCase machine-parseable reason. Maximum permitted length of a reason is 256 bytes.
---@field status string status is the health status category. Possible values are: - "StorageHealthUnknown": the driver reported an unknown health status, or a status Kubernetes does not recognize; the backend must not be considered healthy. - "StorageUnreachable": the storage backend is unreachable. - "StorageDegraded": the storage backend is functioning with reduced capability. - "StorageHealthy": the storage backend is healthy as seen from this node. Additional values may be introduced as the CSI specification evolves. Writers that do not recognize a status may classify it as StorageHealthUnknown. Readers that do not recognize a status must use it only for health reporting and observability.
---@field volumeMode? string volumeMode is the volume mode affected. Nil means both are affected.

---healthConditions are the storage backend conditions reported by the CSI driver. At most 16 conditions may be reported. An empty list means the CSI driver either does not support storage health or has not reported it yet. If the driver supports storage health and its storage backend is healthy, the kubelet reports a StorageHealthy condition.
---@alias kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1StorageHealthHealthConditionsList kubernetes.storage.IoK8sApiStorageV1StorageHealthCondition[]

